Strong real-world example

“Suppose we have 30 microservices. Without Shared Libraries, each Jenkinsfile may contain 100–200 lines of repeated Docker, SonarQube, security scanning and Kubernetes deployment logic. With a Shared Library, we move that common logic into reusable functions. Each microservice Jenkinsfile might only have 30–40 lines. If our security team changes the Trivy scanning requirement, we update the shared function once and all pipelines can use the updated implementation.”

